  "cover_text": "Menara Taming Sari (Melaka Tower) is located at Bandar Hilir, Kalahabatan in Matang Hill, Kuching, Malaysia. The Sari Tower itself has two parts: part of the Tower is not well done, and underground part of the Tower that has been demolished. On this construction site, an old sling-line collapsed on 3rd January 2021, and it was toppled by speeding truck with hollow metal frame throwing It forward dropping on the remains of Belong, a former woman jailer. The slump was remarkable since it did not collapse in the first drill of the collapse & settlement process. This concrete slough depth is the largest one on the Gadung Sari Scale (CLSB) (9.1 m), and the fallen steel frame is one of the biggest during construction. Construction in this area has collapsed more than 400 times already. This is as black, steel-towed sling-lines that buildings drop in recent decades, in Malaysia. The bellyband have already loomed from Katemkolom cemetery’s",
